# Milestone: M3 / activated v0.10.14
# Covers: a loop with a backward OP_JMP exercises the safepoint on each
#         iteration; the safepoint decrements safepoint_budget_remaining
#         and the step budget, preventing infinite-loop starvation.
#         Behavioral correctness: the loop completes and produces the
#         expected result (5).  The backward-branch decrement itself is
#         internal and not observable from pure urbiscript.  Its EFFECT is
#         covered in C by
#         tests/rt/test_api.c::the_configured_step_budget_bounds_an_unbudgeted_step,
#         which is a loop that outruns a one-instruction budget -- and a
#         loop can only do that because its back-edge is what spends it.
#         The decrement site is uexec_ops.c's sole budget decrement; no
#         case reads the counter directly.

var i = 0; while (i < 5) { i = i + 1 }; i
[00000000] 5
